---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Adding Movies"
  description="Add movies to your NGMS library and configure automatic release monitoring."
  section="how-to"
  prev={{ title: 'Adding Series',     href: '/how-to/adding-series' }}
  next={{ title: 'Import Pipeline',   href: '/how-to/import-pipeline' }}
>

<h1>Adding Movies</h1>
<p class="page-meta">The flow is the same as series — no episode structure to worry about.</p>

<h2>Adding a movie</h2>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">1</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Movies → Add Movie</h3>
    <p>Search by title. NGMS queries TMDB and shows posters, release year, and runtime.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">2</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Configure</h3>
    <p>Set <strong>Quality Profile</strong>, <strong>Root Folder</strong>, and
    <strong>Monitored</strong> toggle. If monitored, NGMS will search for the movie automatically
    once it passes its release date.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="step">
  <div class="step-num">3</div>
  <div class="step-body">
    <h3>Add</h3>
    <p>
      Click <strong>Add Movie</strong>. If the movie is already past its release date and you
      enabled monitoring, NGMS queues an immediate search. Otherwise it waits for the release
      date (checked daily via the scheduler).
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Availability thresholds</h2>

<p>
  NGMS respects TMDB's availability flags. You can configure a <strong>minimum availability</strong>
  threshold per-movie or globally in Settings:
</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Threshold</th><th>When NGMS starts searching</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>Announced</strong></td><td>Immediately after adding (even if months before release)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>In Cinemas</strong></td><td>Once TMDB marks the film as in cinemas</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Released</strong></td><td>Once TMDB marks a digital/physical release (recommended)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Bulk import from lists</h2>

<p>
  NGMS supports adding movies in bulk from sources like the <strong>Plex Watchlist</strong>,
  TMDB lists, or the <strong>Discover</strong> page. From Discover, hover a poster and click
  <strong>Add to Library</strong> to add it with your default profile and root folder.
</p>

<div class="callout callout-note">
  <span class="callout-icon">ℹ</span>
  <div class="callout-body">
    Movies are organized into a single folder per film: <code>/media/movies/Movie Title (2024)/Movie Title (2024).mkv</code>.
    The folder and filename pattern can be customized in <strong>Settings → Media Management → Movie Naming</strong>.
  </div>
</div>

</DocsLayout>
